{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J9X2CfbbweK143u4vTF1Ay","type":"tool_result","content":"# Reference palette\n\nThis is the **reference instance** of the data-viz method: every parameter the\nmethod needs, filled in with a validated default palette. The rest of the skill\nis system-agnostic - **to target your brand, substitute this file's values** and\nre-run the validator. Nothing else changes.\n\n## How to use these values\n\nEverything below is plain hex. In an HTML chart, **define the slots you use as\nCSS custom properties in a local `<style>` block** at the top of the file, then\nreference them by role throughout - so the light/dark values swap in one place,\nand the chart body is written against roles rather than raw hex:\n\n```css\n.viz-root {\n  color-scheme: light;\n  --surface-1:      #fcfcfb;   /* chart surface */\n  --text-primary:   #0b0b0b;\n  --text-secondary: #52514e;\n  --series-1:       #2a78d6;   /* categorical slot 1 */\n  /* ...only the roles this chart uses */\n}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n  :root:where(:not([data-theme=\"light\"])) .viz-root {\n    color-scheme: dark;\n    --surface-1:      #1a1a19;\n    --text-primary:   #f0efec;\n    --text-secondary: #c3c2b7;\n    --series-1:       #3987e5;\n  }\n}\n:root[data-theme=\"dark\"] .viz-root {\n  color-scheme: dark;\n  --surface-1:      #1a1a19;\n  --text-primary:   #f0efec;\n  --text-secondary: #c3c2b7;\n  --series-1:       #3987e5;\n}\n```\n\nDeclare the dark values under both scopes as above - the media query covers\nthe OS setting; the `data-theme` scope covers the viewer's theme toggle,\nwhich must win both ways (the `:not(...)` guard lets a light stamp beat\nOS-dark; `:where()` keeps the media block below the toggle scope).\n\n## Categorical palette\n\nBoth modes are selected. The dark column is the same eight hues stepped for the\ndark surface, not a separate palette:\n\n| Slot | Hue | Light | Dark |\n|------|-----|-------|------|\n| 1 | blue | `#2a78d6` | `#3987e5` |\n| 2 | orange | `#eb6834` | `#d95926` |\n| 3 | aqua | `#1baf7a` | `#199e70` |\n| 4 | yellow | `#eda100` | `#c98500` |\n| 5 | magenta | `#e87ba4` | `#d55181` |\n| 6 | green | `#008300` | `#008300` |\n| 7 | violet | `#6250d6` | `#9085e9` |\n/tmp/claude-25919/bundled-skills/2.1.302/3c3a4ba06ccc17263d3d4f7114fd92b7/dataviz/references/palette.md:155:Triggered by the accessibility setting, pr\n/tmp/claude-25919/bundled-skills/2.1.302/3c3a4ba06ccc17263d3d4f7114fd92b7/dataviz/references/marks-and-anatomy.md:89:Where hue fails - full-severity C\n/tmp/claude-25919/bundled-skills/2.1.302/3c3a4ba06ccc17263d3d4f7114fd92b7/dataviz/references/marks-and-anatomy.md:94:sign) so it never misstates the v\n/tmp/claude-25919/bundled-skills/2.1.302/3c3a4ba06ccc17263d3d4f7114fd92b7/dataviz/references/anti-patterns.md:100:Good: Texture is opt-in (a11y settin\n/tmp/claude-25919/bundled-skills/2.1.302/3c3a4ba06ccc17263d3d4f7114fd92b7/dataviz/references/interaction.md:5:Design it with the same care as the stat\n/tmp/claude-25919/bundled-skills/2.1.302/3c3a4ba06ccc17263d3d4f7114fd92b7/dataviz/references/choosing-a-form.md:42:  for accessibility (full CVD), pri","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b0894c3-d91e-45a5-b742-1e1609c0e675","uuid":"7162217d-9513-4d27-a9d5-ecbffe09d0fe","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:14:07.975Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Reference palette\n\nThis is the **reference instance** of the data-viz method: every parameter the\nmethod needs, filled in with a validated default palette. The rest of the skill\nis system-agnostic - **to target your brand, substitute this file's values** and\nre-run the validator. Nothing else changes.\n\n## How to use these values\n\nEverything below is plain hex. In an HTML chart, **define the slots you use as\nCSS custom properties in a local `<style>` block** at the top of the file, then\nreference them by role throughout - so the light/dark values swap in one place,\nand the chart body is written against roles rather than raw hex:\n\n```css\n.viz-root {\n  color-scheme: light;\n  --surface-1:      #fcfcfb;   /* chart surface */\n  --text-primary:   #0b0b0b;\n  --text-secondary: #52514e;\n  --series-1:       #2a78d6;   /* categorical slot 1 */\n  /* ...only the roles this chart uses */\n}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n  :root:where(:not([data-theme=\"light\"])) .viz-root {\n    color-scheme: dark;\n    --surface-1:      #1a1a19;\n    --text-primary:   #f0efec;\n    --text-secondary: #c3c2b7;\n    --series-1:       #3987e5;\n  }\n}\n:root[data-theme=\"dark\"] .viz-root {\n  color-scheme: dark;\n  --surface-1:      #1a1a19;\n  --text-primary:   #f0efec;\n  --text-secondary: #c3c2b7;\n  --series-1:       #3987e5;\n}\n```\n\nDeclare the dark values under both scopes as above - the media query covers\nthe OS setting; the `data-theme` scope covers the viewer's theme toggle,\nwhich must win both ways (the `:not(...)` guard lets a light stamp beat\nOS-dark; `:where()` keeps the media block below the toggle scope).\n\n## Categorical palette\n\nBoth modes are selected. The dark column is the same eight hues stepped for the\ndark surface, not a separate palette:\n\n| Slot | Hue | Light | Dark |\n|------|-----|-------|------|\n| 1 | blue | `#2a78d6` | `#3987e5` |\n| 2 | orange | `#eb6834` | `#d95926` |\n| 3 | aqua | `#1baf7a` | `#199e70` |\n| 4 | yellow | `#eda100` | `#c98500` |\n| 5 | magenta | `#e87ba4` | `#d55181` |\n| 6 | green | `#008300` | `#008300` |\n| 7 | violet | `#6250d6` | `#9085e9` |\n/tmp/claude-25919/bundled-skills/2.1.302/3c3a4ba06ccc17263d3d4f7114fd92b7/dataviz/references/palette.md:155:Triggered by the accessibility setting, pr\n/tmp/claude-25919/bundled-skills/2.1.302/3c3a4ba06ccc17263d3d4f7114fd92b7/dataviz/references/marks-and-anatomy.md:89:Where hue fails - full-severity C\n/tmp/claude-25919/bundled-skills/2.1.302/3c3a4ba06ccc17263d3d4f7114fd92b7/dataviz/references/marks-and-anatomy.md:94:sign) so it never misstates the v\n/tm