{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZsdxCPw2JUb9HHCD3xN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RmEmXRs1TVoLtmaNxv3e29","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/summereunann/.claude/projects/-data/memory/neurico-escape-sim-lessons.md","content":"---\nname: neurico-escape-sim-lessons\ndescription: Lessons from small-network optimizer dynamics runs on the shared neurico host (GPU vs CPU cost, quench/basin definition audits, saddle choice)\nmetadata:\n  type: reference\n---\n\nObserved 2026-10-30 (sgd_escape_time_distributions workspace, no LLM, no resource-finder output). See [[neurico-host-local-llm-fallback]].\n\n- Batched replica simulators (R×P tensors, hand-derived backprop) fit 1–3 GB GPU slices. Full-batch gradients were ~25× faster on a contended GPU than on 2 CPU cores, so 7–9 workers on saturated GPUs still did ~40 jobs/h; R=256 × 2,000 samples fits.\n- Workers must wait on OOM, not skip: a worker that moved on burned the whole job list in a minute. Re-reading the job file after each job lets you reprioritize live.\n- Basin-exit tests must be checked for convergence: short quenches changed the verdict from 0–34% to 97%. Then audit exits with exact Newton polish: 7.8% were soft-mode false exits. Chord-Newton with a fixed H*^-1 is unreliable as a verdict (drifts on real minima, wrongly certifies), and \"no segment barrier\" alone is wrong (real barrier-free neighbours exist).\n- Symmetric saddles (unit-zero, unit-duplicate) have zero per-sample gradient along escape directions, so SGD noise can't escape them. Use generic saddles; index-preserving trust-region Newton needs a small net (P≈115 worked, P=290 did not converge) and low-index starts.\n- Weibull extrapolations of heavily censored runs reach 1e9: hold such medians at the observed bound and flag them.\n- `| grep` on a killed foreground job loses the output: log to a file.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12427,"cache_read_input_tokens":285779,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12427},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b0894c3-d91e-45a5-b742-1e1609c0e675","uuid":"1cbeb3e4-ea9f-421e-92eb-7f763bd57f27","timestamp":"2026-10-31T06:53:34.346Z","request_id":"req_011CgZsdwnM8vkuA7cKazENs","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RmEmXRs1TVoLtmaNxv3e29":{"file_path":"/home/summereunann/.claude/projects/-data/memory/neurico-escape-sim-lessons.md","content":"---\nname: neurico-escape-sim-lessons\ndescription: Lessons from small-network optimizer dynamics runs on the shared neurico host (GPU vs CPU cost, quench/basin definition audits, saddle choice)\nmetadata:\n  type: reference\n---\n\nObserved 2026-10-30 (sgd_escape_time_distributions workspace, no LLM, no resource-finder output). See [[neurico-host-local-llm-fallback]].\n\n- Batched replica simulators (R×P tensors, hand-derived backprop) fit 1–3 GB GPU slices. Full-batch gradients were ~25× faster on a contended GPU than on 2 CPU cores, so 7–9 workers on saturated GPUs still did ~40 jobs/h; R=256 × 2,000 samples fits.\n- Workers must wait on OOM, not skip: a worker that moved on burned the whole job list in a minute. Re-reading the job file after each job lets you reprioritize live.\n- Basin-exit tests must be checked for convergence: short quenches changed the verdict from 0–34% to 97%. Then audit exits with exact Newton polish: 7.8% were soft-mode false exits. Chord-Newton with a fixed H*^-1 is unreliable as a verdict (drifts on real minima, wrongly certifies), and \"no segment barrier\" alone is wrong (real barrier-free neighbours exist).\n- Symmetric saddles (unit-zero, unit-duplicate) have zero per-sample gradient along escape directions, so SGD noise can't escape them. Use generic saddles; index-preserving trust-region Newton needs a small net (P≈115 worked, P=290 did not converge) and low-index starts.\n- Weibull extrapolations of heavily censored runs reach 1e9: hold such medians at the observed bound and flag them.\n- `| grep` on a killed foreground job loses the output: log to a file.\n"}}}
