{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZsgtt3v4yhHjz6yLw4N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The research is finished, and none of the four hypothesis claims held as stated, though parts of H1, H2 and H3 did. All phases ran, covering 165 of 166 planned conditions: 23,104 replicas, 17,474 exits and 30 saddles. The one missing job is default-LR Adam at the sharpest minimum, cut off at the time limit.\n\n| Claim | Verdict | Key result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Escape times are Weibull, not exponential | Partly | Exponential rejected in 86% of conditions, but Weibull was best by AIC in only 4 of 28 |\n| Shape k is between 0.7 and 1.3 and depends on geometry | Refuted | Only 32% in range (median 1.47); no correlation with sharpness (ρ = −0.06) |\n| Adam escapes narrow basins 2–5× faster | Partly | 2.75× [1.89, 5.18]; point estimate in range, confidence interval wider |\n| Adam matches SGD at wide basins | Refuted | 1.89× [1.24, 3.22]; no significant narrow/wide difference, but only 4 minima per group |\n| Doubling batch size multiplies τ by √2 | Refuted | ×5.1 [3.4, 8.0] per doubling; τ grows about as B² |\n| η/B sets temperature | Supported on Fashion-MNIST | τ·η ratios 1.05 and 0.94; only partly on digits (1.28 and 0.55, few exits) |\n| Top eigenvector predicts saddle exit 70–85% of the time | Depends on noise | 54% at high noise, 82–86% at low noise (r=1) |\n| Eigenvalue gap predicts that accuracy | Refuted | All correlations non-significant |\n\nThree findings go beyond the hypothesis:\n- **Why k isn't 1:** a start-up delay pushes k above 1, and mixing different minima pushes it below 1. Removing the delay moves median k from 1.47 to 1.03, and pooling minima gives 0.52–0.74.\n- **Adam depends on learning rate:** it's about 2× faster at matched in-basin loss, and the ablations point to adaptive scaling, not momentum. At the default lr=0.001 it never escaped, at any of the 5 minima tested.\n- **Saddle exits are reproducible:** even at high noise, 88% of a saddle's replicas exit in the same direction, often not the top eigenvector. Linear theory doesn't predict that, and I didn't test the cause.\n\n**Validation:**\n- The simulator matches the exact Kramers rate (median ratio 1.07 at high barrier).\n- 98.4% of 192 sampled exits are real, and a same-seed rerun of one condition matched every replica exactly.\n- Testing caught two bugs before they reached results: short quenches gave wrong exit verdicts, and 7.8% of the first 6,337 exits were false. Both are fixed, and affected runs were rerun.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- These are tiny networks (115–610 parameters), so nothing here is shown for deep networks.\n- The saddle results come from a smaller network than the minima results.\n- The 150,000-step cap excludes 8 of 36 conditions from the shape analysis and limits the power-law vs Arrhenius comparison at large batch sizes. Digits replication is weak for the same reason.\n- The saddle exit radius wasn't preregistered, so all radii and noise levels are reported.\n- No literature-review resources had been gathered, so I compiled them here and checked the citations against arXiv. No LLM or API was used, because this study runs real optimizers on real networks.\n- Nothing was committed to git, because `git` refused this directory with an ownership error.\n\nPlan deviations are in `planning.md`. Everything is in the workspace; start with `REPORT.md`, with the overview and reproduction steps in `README.md`. Figures are in `figures/`, and all statistics are in `results/analysis/summary.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4709,"cache_read_input_tokens":298206,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4709},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b0894c3-d91e-45a5-b742-1e1609c0e675","uuid":"937c9fbe-7cd9-4cd5-8483-3bdf42e36413","timestamp":"2026-10-31T06:53:48.628Z","request_id":"req_011CgZsgtdfg6cPk6txkisCM"}
